.TH PWRITE 3crunch "" "Crunch" "Crunch Library Manual"
.SH NAME
pwrite \- write bytes at a file offset
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
.B #include <unistd.h>
.B ssize_t pwrite(int descriptor, const void* buffer, size_t byte_count, off_t offset);
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
Writes bytes at offset without changing the open file's current position.
Writes may be short; the caller must provide sufficient readable storage.
On Linux, O_APPEND causes the write to append regardless of offset.
.SH RETURN VALUE
Returns bytes written, or \-1 with errno set. Success leaves errno unchanged.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR pread (3crunch),
.BR write (3crunch),
.BR pwrite (2)
